  "body": "## What changed\n\nInstall an uncaptured-error handler when the shared GPU device is made.\nUse one failure latch for this handler and the device-loss callback.\nKeep the first reason and log it once.\nLater stock-cut calls use the existing CPU path and return its exact values.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe shared device had a device-loss callback but no uncaptured-error handler.\nAn unscoped validation error reached the default wgpu handler and caused a panic.\n\n## Tests\n\nPin: `shared::tests::shared_device_faults_use_cpu`.\nThe pin runs each fault in an isolated process.\nIt checks real device destruction and an unscoped validation error.\nIt checks repeated CPU calls and retention of the first reason.\nThe unchanged code failed with the wgpu validation panic before the fix.\n\nMutation checks restore the old production code, remove each callback, and bypass the failure-refusal guard.\nAll four mutations fail the pin.\nEach restored fix passes.\n\nFinal checks use upstream/main `0760e54ed` as the base:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-gpu --lib shared::tests::shared_device_faults_use_cpu -- --exact --nocapture`: passed.\n  Both fault paths ran on llvmpipe (LLVM 21.1.8, 256 bits) through Vulkan.\n  Neither path skipped.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed, 3 of 3 steps.\n  The GPU library has 8 passing tests, including the pin.\n  The bin-parity suite has 3 passing tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gpu --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-gpu --test cut_parity`: passed, 9 of 9 tests.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: passed, 0 applicable steps.\n  The planner did not reach 102 steps.\n  GPU changes have no mapped heavy lane.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: passed, 1 of 1 steps.\n  The catalog has 39 passing tests and 4 ignored tests.\n\nThe gate test selector could not discover this library test.\nThe direct cargo command ran the pin, and the quick gate included it.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe catalog suite and GPU cut-parity suite passed.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` returned no changes after those runs.\nNo recorded program required regeneration.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA physical driver reset was not exercised.\nThe loss pin destroys the device through the public wgpu API and polls its callback.\nThe four ignored catalog tests were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changed either file when the overlap check ran.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Shared GPU errors disable compute and retain the CPU fallback instead of causing an uncaptured-error panic.\n\nFixes #3533\n",
